# Copy this file to .env before running `docker compose up --build`.
# Nothing here is required to cost money:
#   - Map: Leaflet.js + OpenStreetMap tiles (no key)
#   - Directions: the public OSRM demo routing API (no key)
#   - AI assistant, local dev: Ollama running natively on your machine (no key)
#   - AI assistant, Render deployment: Groq (free tier, no credit card - see below)

# Which Ollama model the assistant-service asks for when running locally with
# no GROQ_API_KEY set. Defaults to llama3.2:1b (~1.3GB) if unset - picked to
# be realistic on a slow/limited connection. If you have more bandwidth to
# spare, a bigger model (e.g. llama3, ~4.7GB) will generally answer better -
# just set OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3 here and `ollama pull llama3` first.
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:1b

# Optional: set this to make assistant-service use Groq (free, no card,
# very fast) instead of Ollama, even locally. Get a free key at
# console.groq.com - this is also what powers the AI assistant on the Render
# deployment, since Ollama can't run there (see README "Deploying to Render").
# Leave unset for local dev - Ollama is used automatically instead.
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: which Groq model to use. Defaults to llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# (fast and high quality, 1,000 free requests/day) if unset.
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
